<title>FRANCE: Algeria's sea security firm shows profit. [CORRECTED 16:43 GMT]</title>
<headline>Algeria's sea security firm shows profit. [CORRECTED 16:43 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Algeria's state-owned firm Najda Maghreb, specialising in rescue and maritime security, posted a 2.6 million dinar ($48,950) profit in 1995, the official Algerian news agency APS said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Naja Maghreb is based in the western city of Arzew, Algeria's main outlet for gas and oil exports. There were no comparative figures available. ($1=54 dinars)</p>
<p>(Corrects exchange rate).</p>
</text>
